---@alias aws.lex_runtime_v2.RuntimeHintValuesList aws.lex_runtime_v2.RuntimeHintValue[]

---You can provide Amazon Lex V2 with hints to the phrases that a customer is likely to use for a slot. When a slot with hints is resolved, the phrases in the runtime hints are preferred in the resolution. You can provide hints for a maximum of 100 intents. You can provide a maximum of 100 slots.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.RuntimeHints
---@field slotHints? aws.lex_runtime_v2.SlotHintsIntentMap A list of the slots in the intent that should have runtime hints added, and the phrases that should be added for each slot.

---@alias aws.lex_runtime_v2.SensitiveNonEmptyString string

---Provides information about the sentiment expressed in a user's response in a conversation. Sentiments are determined using Amazon Comprehend. Sentiments are only returned if they are enabled for the bot.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.SentimentResponse
---@field sentiment? aws.lex_runtime_v2.SentimentType The overall sentiment expressed in the user's response. This is the sentiment most likely expressed by the user based on the analysis by Amazon Comprehend.
---@field sentimentScore? aws.lex_runtime_v2.SentimentScore

---The individual sentiment responses for the utterance.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.SentimentScore
---@field positive aws.lex_runtime_v2.Double The level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has in the accuracy of its detection of the POSITIVE sentiment.
---@field negative aws.lex_runtime_v2.Double The level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has in the accuracy of its detection of the NEGATIVE sentiment.
---@field neutral aws.lex_runtime_v2.Double The level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has in the accuracy of its detection of the NEUTRAL sentiment.
---@field mixed aws.lex_runtime_v2.Double The level of confidence that Amazon Comprehend has in the accuracy of its detection of the MIXED sentiment.

---@alias aws.lex_runtime_v2.SentimentType "MIXED"|"NEGATIVE"|"NEUTRAL"|"POSITIVE"

---@alias aws.lex_runtime_v2.SessionId string

---The state of the user's session with Amazon Lex V2.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.SessionState
---@field dialogAction? aws.lex_runtime_v2.DialogAction The next step that Amazon Lex V2 should take in the conversation with a user.
---@field intent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.Intent The active intent that Amazon Lex V2 is processing.
---@field activeContexts? aws.lex_runtime_v2.ActiveContextsList One or more contexts that indicate to Amazon Lex V2 the context of a request. When a context is active, Amazon Lex V2 considers intents with the matching context as a trigger as the next intent in a session.
---@field sessionAttributes? aws.lex_runtime_v2.StringMap Map of key/value pairs representing session-specific context information. It contains application information passed between Amazon Lex V2 and a client application.
---@field originatingRequestId? aws.lex_runtime_v2.NonEmptyString A unique identifier for a specific request.
---@field runtimeHints? aws.lex_runtime_v2.RuntimeHints Hints for phrases that a customer is likely to use for a slot. Amazon Lex V2 uses the hints to help determine the correct value of a slot.

---@alias aws.lex_runtime_v2.Shape "Scalar"|"List"|"Composite"

---A value that Amazon Lex V2 uses to fulfill an intent.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.Slot
---@field value? aws.lex_runtime_v2.Value The current value of the slot.
---@field shape? aws.lex_runtime_v2.Shape|string When the shape value is List, it indicates that the values field contains a list of slot values. When the value is Scalar, it indicates that the value field contains a single value.
---@field values? aws.lex_runtime_v2.Values A list of one or more values that the user provided for the slot. For example, if a for a slot that elicits pizza toppings, the values might be "pepperoni" and "pineapple."
---@field subSlots? aws.lex_runtime_v2.Slots The constituent sub slots of a composite slot.

