---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.StartConversationRequest
---@field botId aws.lex_runtime_v2.BotIdentifier The identifier of the bot to process the request.
---@field botAliasId aws.lex_runtime_v2.BotAliasIdentifier The alias identifier in use for the bot that processes the request.
---@field localeId aws.lex_runtime_v2.LocaleId The locale where the session is in use.
---@field sessionId aws.lex_runtime_v2.SessionId The identifier of the user session that is having the conversation.
---@field conversationMode? aws.lex_runtime_v2.ConversationMode|string The conversation type that you are using the Amazon Lex V2. If the conversation mode is AUDIO you can send both audio and DTMF information. If the mode is TEXT you can only send text.
---@field requestEventStream aws.lex_runtime_v2.StartConversationRequestEventStream Represents the stream of events to Amazon Lex V2 from your application. The events are encoded as HTTP/2 data frames.

---Represents a stream of events between your application and Amazon Lex V2.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.StartConversationRequestEventStream
---@field ConfigurationEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.ConfigurationEvent Configuration information sent from your client application to Amazon Lex V2
---@field AudioInputEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.AudioInputEvent Speech audio sent from your client application to Amazon Lex V2. Audio starts accumulating when Amazon Lex V2 identifies a voice and continues until a natural pause in the speech is found before processing.
---@field DTMFInputEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.DTMFInputEvent DTMF information sent to Amazon Lex V2 by your application. Amazon Lex V2 accumulates the DMTF information from when the user sends the first character and ends
---@field TextInputEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.TextInputEvent Text sent from your client application to Amazon Lex V2. Each TextInputEvent is processed individually.
---@field PlaybackCompletionEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.PlaybackCompletionEvent Event sent from the client application to Amazon Lex V2 to indicate that it has finished playing audio and that Amazon Lex V2 should start listening for user input.
---@field DisconnectionEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.DisconnectionEvent Event sent from the client application to indicate to Amazon Lex V2 that the conversation is over.

---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.StartConversationResponse
---@field responseEventStream? aws.lex_runtime_v2.StartConversationResponseEventStream Represents the stream of events from Amazon Lex V2 to your application. The events are encoded as HTTP/2 data frames.

---Represents a stream of events between Amazon Lex V2 and your application.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.StartConversationResponseEventStream
---@field PlaybackInterruptionEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.PlaybackInterruptionEvent
---@field TranscriptEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.TranscriptEvent
---@field IntentResultEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.IntentResultEvent Event sent from Amazon Lex V2 to the client application containing the current state of the conversation between the user and Amazon Lex V2.
---@field TextResponseEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.TextResponseEvent
---@field AudioResponseEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.AudioResponseEvent
---@field HeartbeatEvent? aws.lex_runtime_v2.HeartbeatEvent
---@field AccessDeniedException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.AccessDeniedException Exception thrown when the credentials passed with the request are invalid or expired. Also thrown when the credentials in the request do not have permission to access the StartConversation operation.
---@field ResourceNotFoundException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.ResourceNotFoundException Exception thrown if one of the input parameters points to a resource that does not exist. For example, if the bot ID specified does not exist.
---@field ValidationException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.ValidationException Exception thrown when one or more parameters could not be validated. The message contains the name of the field that isn't valid.
---@field ThrottlingException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.ThrottlingException Exception thrown when your application exceeds the maximum number of concurrent requests.
---@field InternalServerException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.InternalServerException An error occurred with Amazon Lex V2.
---@field ConflictException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.ConflictException Exception thrown when two clients are using the same AWS account, Amazon Lex V2 bot, and session ID.
---@field DependencyFailedException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.DependencyFailedException
---@field BadGatewayException? aws.lex_runtime_v2.BadGatewayException

