---@alias aws.lex_runtime_v2.Text string

---The event sent from your client application to Amazon Lex V2 with text input from the user.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.TextInputEvent
---@field text aws.lex_runtime_v2.Text|distilled.Secret The text from the user. Amazon Lex V2 processes this as a complete statement.
---@field eventId? aws.lex_runtime_v2.EventId A unique identifier that your application assigns to the event. You can use this to identify events in logs.
---@field clientTimestampMillis? aws.lex_runtime_v2.EpochMillis A timestamp set by the client of the date and time that the event was sent to Amazon Lex V2.

---The event sent from Amazon Lex V2 to your application with text to present to the user.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.TextResponseEvent
---@field messages? aws.lex_runtime_v2.Messages A list of messages to send to the user. Messages are ordered based on the order that you returned the messages from your Lambda function or the order that the messages are defined in the bot.
---@field eventId? aws.lex_runtime_v2.EventId A unique identifier of the event sent by Amazon Lex V2. The identifier is in the form RESPONSE-N, where N is a number starting with one and incremented for each event sent by Amazon Lex V2 in the current session.

---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.ThrottlingException
---@field message aws.lex_runtime_v2.String

---Event sent from Amazon Lex V2 to your client application that contains a transcript of voice audio.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.TranscriptEvent
---@field transcript? aws.lex_runtime_v2.String The transcript of the voice audio from the user.
---@field eventId? aws.lex_runtime_v2.EventId A unique identifier of the event sent by Amazon Lex V2. The identifier is in the form RESPONSE-N, where N is a number starting with one and incremented for each event sent by Amazon Lex V2 in the current session.

---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.ValidationException
---@field message aws.lex_runtime_v2.String

---Information about the value provided for a slot and Amazon Lex V2's interpretation.
---@class aws.lex_runtime_v2.Value
---@field originalValue? aws.lex_runtime_v2.NonEmptyString The part of the user's response to the slot elicitation that Amazon Lex V2 determines is relevant to the slot value.
---@field interpretedValue aws.lex_runtime_v2.NonEmptyString The value that Amazon Lex V2 determines for the slot, given the user input. The actual value depends on the setting of the value selection strategy for the bot. You can choose to use the value entered by the user, or you can have Amazon Lex V2 choose the first value in the resolvedValues list.
---@field resolvedValues? aws.lex_runtime_v2.StringList A list of values that Amazon Lex V2 determines are possible resolutions for the user input. The first value matches the interpretedValue.

---@alias aws.lex_runtime_v2.Values aws.lex_runtime_v2.Slot[]

